<decision #track.topological_decision_questions.frontier_batches { status = "accepted" blocks = [] durable_candidate = true } (
  <question ?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74B>
  How should planning ask a decision forest with multiple roots?
  </?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74B>
  <answer ?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74C>
  Ask every independently answerable root or unlocked child in one bounded topological batch, then recompute after the response.
  </?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74C>
  <evidence ?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74D>
  The requested protocol must avoid serialising unrelated decision directions while retaining dependency order.
  </?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74D>
  <confidence ?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74E>
  0.99
  </?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74E>
  <reversibility ?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74F>
  moderate
  </?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74F>
)>

<decision #track.enable_modeling_and_atomic_archive.default_enablement { priority = "P0" status = "accepted" durable_candidate = true confidence = 0.99 reversibility = "easy" } (
  <question ?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74G>
  Modeling 的默认启用语义是什么？
  </?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74G>
  <recommendation ?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74H>
